                                   128's layout and feel, and from which I
                                   borrowed the name.

Abraham Ezekowitz <aezekowitz@gmail.com> - several nature photographs which I
                                           converted to create the backdrop
                                           images for C128 "hires" mode.

Desiree Vie < > - several photographs of Niagara Falls, which I converted into
                  backdrop images for C128 "hires" mode.

John Catraham <catraham.john@gmx.net> - painted the the supernova/planet image
                                        from which I generated catraham.xpm
                                        (yet another of the C128 "hires"
                                        mode backdrops)

NASA - Their Hubble Space Telescope took pictures of the Whirlpool Galaxy, the
       Omega Nebula, and the Hodge nebula, which I converted for use as 
       C128 "hires" mode backdrop images.

I ported the following skins from XMMS and/or WinAMP:

Expensive High-Fi: Original by Will Mooney <wsmooney@hotmail.com>
         NoerdAMP: Original by Hans Karlsson <d98hk@efd.lth.se>
CX2 (Concept-X 2): Original by Espen Thooring <espen@bjorli.com>
           XawMMS: Original by Christopher Allen <cpcallen@ruah.dyndns.org>
          Cracked: Original artist unknown.
             Ions: Original artist unknown.

The "Default" skin is my own design, based loosely on the XawMMS skin.  It 
is intended to trade asthetics for good compression, but still be 
useable in a pinch, that's why it's so ugly. :-)
